.th BX IV 23/1/78
.sh NAME
.bd bx
- BURROUGHS communications link
.sh DESCRIPTION
The files
.it bcr, blp, bfiles?
etc. refer to "stations" on the BURROUGHS TD800 POLL/SELECT multi-drop
communications link.
They behave like unidirectional Unix files
(\ 512 byte writes are the most efficient\ ),
but reads should always be 512 bytes,
as any data not taken from a read message are discarded.
.sh FILES
 for reading: /dev/bcr /dev/bfilesf /dev/bttyf
 for writing: /dev/blp /dev/bfilest /dev/bttyt
.sh "SEE ALSO"
bpr(I)
.sh AUTHOR
Piers Lauder ( University of Sydney )
.sh BUGS
